{
  "_name": "t76_schedule_tx_anchor",
  "_desc": "Regression for the on-air schedule-countdown correction (apply_schedule_tx_fixup). pack_schedule_record stamps the visit-window countdown at beacon BUILD time, but the frame is sent later (LBT defer) and travels one airtime before the receiver records heard_ms (= RX-complete) -- both shift the receiver's window anchor LATE (measured ~+400ms mean on s15). gw_a is home on L1 and visits L2 (10s period, 4s window). At the actual self:tx instant the gateway re-stamps the countdown byte against (tx_now + airtime) so a receiver's heard_ms + countdown lands on the true window open. Verify: gw_a emits schedule_tx_anchor (the fixup ran on a gateway beacon, carrying airtime_ms + per-record build/tx countdown) AND cross-layer traffic from the visit-layer node still reaches l1_dst (no regression vs t73's schedule-defer path).",
